# Every iteration of an unrolled loop trusts what the loop's entry checks have found. With testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime and testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime the walk adds checks to each iteration,
# and an iteration that holds such checks is not unrolled, so no unrolled loop ever ran in those test lanes. With testing=CheckBoundsInEmittersOnly the walk adds nothing,
# the loop is unrolled as in an executable, and each access checks the facts that it was given against memory.
# Next to an array whose accesses are within its own length, the other array has its indexing type read at the entry, and each read of that array branches on the bit.
# Fault injection, testing=SkipUnrollEntryChecks: the bit is inverted, whatever array is passed.
